Request Time: 0 seconds
{"Success":true,"Data":[{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"96.48.159.21","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":79580,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":2,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"d330899f63a31a2aa33f93a444722032","RawContent":"Ok I have to start off by saying how gorgeous you look in your wedding dress! I love the bottom and the sweetheart neckline looks great on you. And $650? That&#039;s a steal!\n\n\nI love the how organized you are! My family bought me a wedding iPad to keep me organized (they know my type A personality too well lol). I&#039;m gonna prep my wedding binder soon with all the receipts and correspondences. I&#039;ll bring that to Mexico with us.\n\n\nI love your ceremony location! And your colours are gorgeous (mine are pretty similar to yours, grey and coral). It&#039;s gonna be such a romantic colour scheme \u263a\ufe0f\n\n\nAs for your parents, I&#039;m sure they&#039;ll behave themselves for your sake!","Attachments":[],"Id":1904638,"PostDate":1442207140,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                Ok I have to start off by saying how gorgeous you look in your wedding dress! I love the bottom and the sweetheart neckline looks great on you. And $650? That's a steal!<br><br>\nI love the how organized you are! My family bought me a wedding iPad to keep me organized (they know my type A personality too well lol). I'm gonna prep my wedding binder soon with all the receipts and correspondences. I'll bring that to Mexico with us.<br><br>\nI love your ceremony location! And your colours are gorgeous (mine are pretty similar to yours, grey and coral). It's gonna be such a romantic colour scheme \u263a\ufe0f<br><br>\nAs for your parents, I'm sure they'll behave themselves for your sake! \r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"My planning thread: <a  class=\"bbc_url\" href=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79425-wafflesmom-moon-palace-planning-thread-january-23-2016\/\">http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79425-wafflesmom-moon-palace-planning-thread-january-23-2016\/<\/a><br><br>\n<p><a  class=\"bbc_url\" href=\"http:\/\/www.TickerFactory.com\/\"><img src=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;4;484\/st\/20160123\/e\/Our+Wedding\/dt\/-2\/k\/44c5\/event.png\" alt=\"event.png\"><\/a>","Email":"jerilee.valenzuela@shaw.ca","IpAddress":"24.114.26.77","GroupId":3,"GroupName":"Member","JoinDate":1410102185,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-279721.jpg?_r=1454805895","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":200,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"Wafflesmom","Id":279721,"Name":"Wafflesmom","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"80.42.248.58","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":79580,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":1,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"1a5b9d4559708d05367fb6dfff5ee25c","RawContent":"Sorry I&#039;m a bit late jumping on the band wagon but...Wow! I love your story! It&#039;s amazing when you &#039;just know&#039;. \n\n\nLove your dress, you look stunning and with that beautiful setting everything will be gorgeous xx\n\n\nMaybeoneday\n\n14 \/10\/2015 - R R C, Mexico","Attachments":[],"Id":1904646,"PostDate":1442212898,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                Sorry I'm a bit late jumping on the band wagon but...Wow! I love your story! It's amazing when you 'just know'. <br><br>\nLove your dress, you look stunning and with that beautiful setting everything will be gorgeous xx<br><br>\nMaybeoneday<br>\n14 \/10\/2015 - R R C, Mexico\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"shelina_nessa@yahoo.co.uk","IpAddress":"149.254.56.238","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1421825139,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":false,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_images\/destination\/profile\/default_large.png","PhotoWidth":125,"PhotoHeight":125,"PhotoType":""},"FormattedName":"maybeoneday","Id":281816,"Name":"maybeoneday","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"66.241.131.23","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":79580,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":2,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"6a789694bf1548ea864931a50f7e064e","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;Girl, you look amazing in that dress. It was made for you!! :)&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Love your pick for the veil.. I was the exact same way. I said so many times \"I don&#039;t want a veil\". I tried a veil.. and I ended up having to have one for the ceremony. I&#039;m switching to a floral crown for the reception, but I think the veil is going to look so pretty and romantic :)&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1904652,"PostDate":1442238165,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>Girl, you look amazing in that dress. It was made for you!! <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Love your pick for the veil.. I was the exact same way. I said so many times \"I don't want a veil\". I tried a veil.. and I ended up having to have one for the ceremony. I'm switching to a floral crown for the reception, but I think the veil is going to look so pretty and romantic <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p>\u00a0<br><br><span style=\"color:#808080;\"><span style=\"font-size:14px;\">My planning thread :<\/span><\/span><br><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78755-perianjay-planning-thread-december-15-2015-beach-palace\/#entry1885631'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78755-perianjay-planning-thread-december-15-2015-beach-palace\/#entry1885631<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><br><br>\n\u00a0","Email":"perianjohnson@gmail.com","IpAddress":"66.241.131.23","GroupId":42,"GroupName":"Sr. Member","JoinDate":1419441414,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-281478.jpg?_r=1453235488","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"perianjay","Id":281478,"Name":"perianjay","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"206.200.253.205","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":79580,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":1,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"e60030741ce2f80165d380fc16b09326","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;Aww I absolutely love your story and it&#039;s more evidence of things happen for a reason!!&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Love your dress and you look amazing in it!!!&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1904665,"PostDate":1442253095,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>Aww I absolutely love your story and it's more evidence of things happen for a reason!!\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Love your dress and you look amazing in it!!!<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p>Daisy<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Can't wait to marry my best friend \u00a0 <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/>.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Planning Thread:\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79500-janjins-planning-thread-azul-sensatori\/?p=1902797'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79500-janjins-planning-thread-azul-sensatori\/?p=1902797<\/a>","Email":"daisy.pitre@gmail.com","IpAddress":"142.255.87.125","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1414964723,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":false,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_images\/destination\/profile\/default_large.png","PhotoWidth":125,"PhotoHeight":125,"PhotoType":""},"FormattedName":"Janjin","Id":280967,"Name":"Janjin","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"207.134.141.162","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":79580,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":2,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"e16ce3e38a96952e7ce863a6af5acc9e","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;@[member=\"acw271011\"] - Thank you so much!!! &amp;nbsp;I agree about the colour change, buffet &amp;amp; paint-change to the ceremony location... Everything is coming together :) &amp;nbsp;Thanks for the note about my Mom... I get her emotions, but it&#039;s hard for me to see why she can&#039;t just put it aside for one day. &amp;nbsp;Hoping she&#039;ll surprise me and everything will be fine. &amp;nbsp;I mentioned you in a comment on the GTA meet-up post - were you able to put the room in that bar near your work on hold for Oct 2? &amp;nbsp;I can&#039;t wait to meet everyone!&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;@[member=\"Wafflesmom\"] - Thank you :) &amp;nbsp;I love my dress so much! &amp;nbsp;The price was such a bonus! &amp;nbsp;I have to stay organized, it was killing me not to be haha, if you&#039;re like me you&#039;ll feel like a weight has come off your shoulders, but it also put into perspective how much I still have to do! &amp;nbsp;Fingers crossed on my parents! &amp;nbsp;I&#039;m not worried about my Dad, my Mom is the feisty one, but my girlfriends promised to help diffuse if necessary.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;@[member=\"maybeoneday\"] - &amp;nbsp;Thank you! &amp;nbsp;Us North Americans love a good English accent&amp;nbsp; ;)&amp;nbsp; And thank you for your comments!&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;@[member=\"perianjay\"] - Ahhhh thank you! &amp;nbsp;I&#039;m so in love with my dress I want to wear it everyday! &amp;nbsp;All the girls I show that know me say \"That dress is so you\". &amp;nbsp;I think with the veil thing, it was just easy to picture without because it&#039;s a tropical setting, but I know what you mean - once you put it on, the game changes. &amp;nbsp;I love that it&#039;s my best friend&#039;s mom&#039;s veil too, it makes it so special. &amp;nbsp;And it&#039;s so simple, which is perfect with the bottom of my dress being so dramatic.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;@[member=\"Janjin\"] - Thank you&amp;nbsp; :)&amp;nbsp;Who knew being thrown into a pool would change my life forever! &amp;nbsp;Thank you so much for the comment about my dress! &amp;nbsp;It has some similarities to yours! &amp;nbsp;Great minds!&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1904666,"PostDate":1442253239,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>@<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"232000\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/232000-acw271011\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">acw271011<\/span><\/a> - Thank you so much!!! \u00a0I agree about the colour change, buffet & paint-change to the ceremony location... Everything is coming together <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/> \u00a0Thanks for the note about my Mom... I get her emotions, but it's hard for me to see why she can't just put it aside for one day. \u00a0Hoping she'll surprise me and everything will be fine. \u00a0I mentioned you in a comment on the GTA meet-up post - were you able to put the room in that bar near your work on hold for Oct 2? \u00a0I can't wait to meet everyone!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>@<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"279721\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/279721-wafflesmom\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">Wafflesmom<\/span><\/a> - Thank you <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/> \u00a0I love my dress so much! \u00a0The price was such a bonus! \u00a0I have to stay organized, it was killing me not to be haha, if you're like me you'll feel like a weight has come off your shoulders, but it also put into perspective how much I still have to do! \u00a0Fingers crossed on my parents! \u00a0I'm not worried about my Dad, my Mom is the feisty one, but my girlfriends promised to help diffuse if necessary.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>@<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"281816\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/281816-maybeoneday\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">maybeoneday<\/span><\/a> - \u00a0Thank you! \u00a0Us North Americans love a good English accent\u00a0 <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/wink.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=';)' \/>\u00a0 And thank you for your comments!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>@<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"281478\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/281478-perianjay\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">perianjay<\/span><\/a> - Ahhhh thank you! \u00a0I'm so in love with my dress I want to wear it everyday! \u00a0All the girls I show that know me say \"That dress is so you\". \u00a0I think with the veil thing, it was just easy to picture without because it's a tropical setting, but I know what you mean - once you put it on, the game changes. \u00a0I love that it's my best friend's mom's veil too, it makes it so special. \u00a0And it's so simple, which is perfect with the bottom of my dress being so dramatic.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>@<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"280967\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/280967-janjin\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">Janjin<\/span><\/a> - Thank you\u00a0 <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/>\u00a0Who knew being thrown into a pool would change my life forever! \u00a0Thank you so much for the comment about my dress! \u00a0It has some similarities to yours! \u00a0Great minds!<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<div><img src=\"http:\/\/\" alt=\"\"><\/div>\n<div><br><div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div><a  class=\"bbc_url\" href=\"http:\/\/www.TickerFactory.com\/\"><img src=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;10731;0\/st\/20160423\/e\/we+leave+for+Mexico%21\/k\/c059\/event.png\" alt=\"event.png\"><\/a>\u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0<a  class=\"bbc_url\" href=\"http:\/\/www.TickerFactory.com\/\"><img src=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;32;116\/st\/20160430\/e\/we+say+I+do%21\/k\/8afc\/event.png\" alt=\"event.png\"><\/a><\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>My Planning Thread:<\/p>\n<p><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79580-deecols-planning-thread-gbp-april-30th-2016\/#entry1904529'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79580-deecols-planning-thread-gbp-april-30th-2016\/#entry1904529<\/a>","Email":"deannaproteau@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"207.134.141.162","GroupId":3,"GroupName":"Member","JoinDate":1421446169,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-281751.jpg?_r=1455392044","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":222,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"deecol","Id":281751,"Name":"deecol","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"207.134.141.162","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":79580,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":5,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"02cd6ed16bdc823eca6d0f0202408859","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Flowers&lt;\/u&gt;&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;...Well, some of the flowers.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;In May I went to Michaels and found these gorgeous flowers! &amp;nbsp;They feel almost real and have that simple, romantic feel I&#039;m after. &amp;nbsp;As I&#039;m very Type A, I decided from the start that I was going to have fake flowers for my bouquets and&amp;nbsp;boutonni\u00e8res, it sounds really bad but it&#039;s one more thing I can have control of.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I found these on sale from $5.99\/flower reduced to $2.39\/flower and my best friend got me her 15% teachers discount. &amp;nbsp;I decided on 5 flowers in each bouquet (me and two bridesmaids) and then once i got my girls dresses I would add to mine based on those colours. &amp;nbsp;So in the end, 15 flowers cost me $35 and that&#039;s 2 1\/2 bouquets sorted. &amp;nbsp;I plan to either tie them with a single thick ribbon in white or to somehow fuse them all together with glue or something so it has that \"just picked these from the garden\" look.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;This is the lovely associate holding three of the flowers against her shirt because at the time I was thinking about our previous red colour scheme.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;A few months later I was in Michael&#039;s again... aka my second home... and found these beautiful boutonni\u00e8res&amp;nbsp;for the guys. &amp;nbsp;We needed 5 total (Col, 2 groomsmen and our dads). &amp;nbsp;They were $4.99 each, I used a 50% discount coupon on one and my friends teachers discount on the whole purchase, all 5 came to about $20.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I still have to get the rest of my bouquet, the mothers corsages, my aisle flowers, and sort out the reception and ceremony flowers with the WC. &amp;nbsp;Shouldn&#039;t be too much as I&#039;m planning to keep really simple. &amp;nbsp;Will be swinging by Michael&#039;s sometime this week, as&amp;nbsp;@[member=\"yycbride2016\"] reminded me there is a fall decoration sale! &amp;nbsp;And I seem to be finding stuff when I&#039;m not necessarily looking - my dress, the flowers, Colin... lol &amp;nbsp;So hoping to keep up this momentum and pop into Michael&#039;s every so often with no direct intentions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1904743,"PostDate":1442327915,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p><strong><u>Flowers<\/u><\/strong><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>...Well, some of the flowers.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>In May I went to Michaels and found these gorgeous flowers! \u00a0They feel almost real and have that simple, romantic feel I'm after. \u00a0As I'm very Type A, I decided from the start that I was going to have fake flowers for my bouquets and\u00a0boutonni\u00e8res, it sounds really bad but it's one more thing I can have control of.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I found these on sale from $5.99\/flower reduced to $2.39\/flower and my best friend got me her 15% teachers discount. \u00a0I decided on 5 flowers in each bouquet (me and two bridesmaids) and then once i got my girls dresses I would add to mine based on those colours. \u00a0So in the end, 15 flowers cost me $35 and that's 2 1\/2 bouquets sorted. \u00a0I plan to either tie them with a single thick ribbon in white or to somehow fuse them all together with glue or something so it has that \"just picked these from the garden\" look.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>This is the lovely associate holding three of the flowers against her shirt because at the time I was thinking about our previous red colour scheme.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><a class='resized_img' rel='lightbox[1904743]' id='ipb-attach-url-' href=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_09_2015\/post-281751-0-31862700-1442323317.jpg\" title=\"Flowers.jpg -  17.38KB\"><img itemprop=\"image\" src=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_09_2015\/post-281751-0-31862700-1442323317.jpg\" class='bbc_img linked-image' alt=\"Flowers.jpg\" \/><\/a>\n\n<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>A few months later I was in Michael's again... aka my second home... and found these beautiful boutonni\u00e8res\u00a0for the guys. \u00a0We needed 5 total (Col, 2 groomsmen and our dads). \u00a0They were $4.99 each, I used a 50% discount coupon on one and my friends teachers discount on the whole purchase, all 5 came to about $20.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><a class='resized_img' rel='lightbox[1904743]' id='ipb-attach-url-' href=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_09_2015\/post-281751-0-79166300-1442323634.jpg\" title=\"Boutonnieres.JPG -  47.81KB\"><img itemprop=\"image\" src=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_09_2015\/post-281751-0-79166300-1442323634.jpg\" class='bbc_img linked-image' alt=\"Boutonnieres.JPG\" \/><\/a>\n\n<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I still have to get the rest of my bouquet, the mothers corsages, my aisle flowers, and sort out the reception and ceremony flowers with the WC. \u00a0Shouldn't be too much as I'm planning to keep really simple. \u00a0Will be swinging by Michael's sometime this week, as\u00a0@<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"283167\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/283167-yycbride2016\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">yycbride2016<\/span><\/a> reminded me there is a fall decoration sale! \u00a0And I seem to be finding stuff when I'm not necessarily looking - my dress, the flowers, Colin... lol \u00a0So hoping to keep up this momentum and pop into Michael's every so often with no direct intentions.\u00a0<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<div><img src=\"http:\/\/\" alt=\"\"><\/div>\n<div><br><div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div><a  class=\"bbc_url\" href=\"http:\/\/www.TickerFactory.com\/\"><img src=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;10731;0\/st\/20160423\/e\/we+leave+for+Mexico%21\/k\/c059\/event.png\" alt=\"event.png\"><\/a>\u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0<a  class=\"bbc_url\" href=\"http:\/\/www.TickerFactory.com\/\"><img src=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;32;116\/st\/20160430\/e\/we+say+I+do%21\/k\/8afc\/event.png\" alt=\"event.png\"><\/a><\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>My Planning Thread:<\/p>\n<p><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79580-deecols-planning-thread-gbp-april-30th-2016\/#entry1904529'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79580-deecols-planning-thread-gbp-april-30th-2016\/#entry1904529<\/a>","Email":"deannaproteau@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"207.134.141.162","GroupId":3,"GroupName":"Member","JoinDate":1421446169,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-281751.jpg?_r=1455392044","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":222,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"deecol","Id":281751,"Name":"deecol","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"66.241.131.23","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":79580,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":4,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"df8d842073cf99466714972f498f93c2","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;Nice! I went with real touch flowers as well and i&#039;m really happy i&#039;m going that route. It was so inexpensive compared to the quotes I received from anyone in Mexico.&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I wanted Peonies specifically and that was the only flower I wanted.. They quoted me $400+ for my bouquet. Just mine!&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I&#039;ve ordered my real touch floral from an Etsy seller who is making me 3 BM bouquets (tied with jute ribbon - looks like burlap), my bouquet (also tied with jute), 7 boutonnieres, 1 wrist corsage and 4 aisle runner bouquets. I&#039;m paying about $150 USD for it all.&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Unreal!&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I like the way your floral looks!! What are you thinking for your own bouquet?&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1904745,"PostDate":1442328914,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>Nice! I went with real touch flowers as well and i'm really happy i'm going that route. It was so inexpensive compared to the quotes I received from anyone in Mexico.\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I wanted Peonies specifically and that was the only flower I wanted.. They quoted me $400+ for my bouquet. Just mine!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I've ordered my real touch floral from an Etsy seller who is making me 3 BM bouquets (tied with jute ribbon - looks like burlap), my bouquet (also tied with jute), 7 boutonnieres, 1 wrist corsage and 4 aisle runner bouquets. I'm paying about $150 USD for it all.\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Unreal!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I like the way your floral looks!! What are you thinking for your own bouquet?<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p>\u00a0<br><br><span style=\"color:#808080;\"><span style=\"font-size:14px;\">My planning thread :<\/span><\/span><br><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78755-perianjay-planning-thread-december-15-2015-beach-palace\/#entry1885631'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78755-perianjay-planning-thread-december-15-2015-beach-palace\/#entry1885631<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><br><br>\n\u00a0","Email":"perianjohnson@gmail.com","IpAddress":"66.241.131.23","GroupId":42,"GroupName":"Sr. Member","JoinDate":1419441414,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-281478.jpg?_r=1453235488","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"perianjay","Id":281478,"Name":"perianjay","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"207.134.141.162","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":79580,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":1,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"ae1dde000f67e8fe6de3a6225edb8faa","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;@[member=\"perianjay\"] That&#039;s a great price for all your flowers! &amp;nbsp;I agree, the flowers in Mexico can be really pricey, and sometimes what you have envisioned isn&#039;t available because of the season. &amp;nbsp;I went to a wedding 5 years ago in Cuba and I remember hearing that the pink bouquets she chose weren&#039;t the same pink she ordered. &amp;nbsp;It wasn&#039;t a big deal in the larger scheme of things because it was the only pink in her whole wedding decor so it was fine, but what if it did need to be a specific shade? &amp;nbsp;That&#039;s what made me want to opt for the fake flowers.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;For my bouquet, because Colin wants a light pink tie and the idea is to have the groomsmen in coral pink ties to match the bridesmaids dresses - I still need to post these! - I would like to find roses (both tight and full opening) in both light and coral. &amp;nbsp;I&#039;ve pinned some examples from pinterest and I think because we are using different shades of pink instead of one, I can get away with everything not all matching the one colour. &amp;nbsp;And the same with the aisle flowers - small bouquets of roses. Do you think that sounds good?&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1904748,"PostDate":1442329916,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>@<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"281478\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/281478-perianjay\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">perianjay<\/span><\/a> That's a great price for all your flowers! \u00a0I agree, the flowers in Mexico can be really pricey, and sometimes what you have envisioned isn't available because of the season. \u00a0I went to a wedding 5 years ago in Cuba and I remember hearing that the pink bouquets she chose weren't the same pink she ordered. \u00a0It wasn't a big deal in the larger scheme of things because it was the only pink in her whole wedding decor so it was fine, but what if it did need to be a specific shade? \u00a0That's what made me want to opt for the fake flowers.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>For my bouquet, because Colin wants a light pink tie and the idea is to have the groomsmen in coral pink ties to match the bridesmaids dresses - I still need to post these! - I would like to find roses (both tight and full opening) in both light and coral. \u00a0I've pinned some examples from pinterest and I think because we are using different shades of pink instead of one, I can get away with everything not all matching the one colour. \u00a0And the same with the aisle flowers - small bouquets of roses. Do you think that sounds good?<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<div><img src=\"http:\/\/\" alt=\"\"><\/div>\n<div><br><div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div><a  class=\"bbc_url\" href=\"http:\/\/www.TickerFactory.com\/\"><img src=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;10731;0\/st\/20160423\/e\/we+leave+for+Mexico%21\/k\/c059\/event.png\" alt=\"event.png\"><\/a>\u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0<a  class=\"bbc_url\" href=\"http:\/\/www.TickerFactory.com\/\"><img src=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;32;116\/st\/20160430\/e\/we+say+I+do%21\/k\/8afc\/event.png\" alt=\"event.png\"><\/a><\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>My Planning Thread:<\/p>\n<p><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79580-deecols-planning-thread-gbp-april-30th-2016\/#entry1904529'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79580-deecols-planning-thread-gbp-april-30th-2016\/#entry1904529<\/a>","Email":"deannaproteau@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"207.134.141.162","GroupId":3,"GroupName":"Member","JoinDate":1421446169,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-281751.jpg?_r=1455392044","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":222,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"deecol","Id":281751,"Name":"deecol","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"66.241.131.23","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":79580,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":3,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"5e23433a14d2405c60239cf99d8d12cc","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;@[member=\"deecol\"] Your vision sounds great. I love the idea of roses. My colour scheme started as coral and gold, but I definitely strayed and once I started understanding more about weddings (my friend is a wedding planner) I realized that the dramatic colours (Coral) don&#039;t need to be used too much. So i&#039;ve decided to use it as more of an accent tone. I think i&#039;m only using coral for my BM dresses\/GM neck ties and the rest of my decor is light blush and light champagne gold. Originally I wanted my centre pieces to be all colours of pink, but now i&#039;ve opted out and i&#039;m going for a classic white rose (about 6 per centrepiece).&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Sometimes less with colours can be more :)&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I think I read that you have metallics in your colour scheme (silver?). How do you plan on incorporating those?! I&#039;m so excited to see your vision unfold :)&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1904753,"PostDate":1442331174,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>@<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"281751\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/281751-deecol\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">deecol<\/span><\/a> Your vision sounds great. I love the idea of roses. My colour scheme started as coral and gold, but I definitely strayed and once I started understanding more about weddings (my friend is a wedding planner) I realized that the dramatic colours (Coral) don't need to be used too much. So i've decided to use it as more of an accent tone. I think i'm only using coral for my BM dresses\/GM neck ties and the rest of my decor is light blush and light champagne gold. Originally I wanted my centre pieces to be all colours of pink, but now i've opted out and i'm going for a classic white rose (about 6 per centrepiece).<\/p>\n<p>Sometimes less with colours can be more <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I think I read that you have metallics in your colour scheme (silver?). How do you plan on incorporating those?! I'm so excited to see your vision unfold <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p>\u00a0<br><br><span style=\"color:#808080;\"><span style=\"font-size:14px;\">My planning thread :<\/span><\/span><br><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78755-perianjay-planning-thread-december-15-2015-beach-palace\/#entry1885631'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78755-perianjay-planning-thread-december-15-2015-beach-palace\/#entry1885631<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><br><br>\n\u00a0","Email":"perianjohnson@gmail.com","IpAddress":"66.241.131.23","GroupId":42,"GroupName":"Sr. Member","JoinDate":1419441414,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-281478.jpg?_r=1453235488","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"perianjay","Id":281478,"Name":"perianjay","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"207.134.141.162","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":79580,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":1442332506,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":2,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"fc9660bdbc9f9bcc8a9c59a4b520bd08","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;@[member=\"perianjay\"] I absolutely agree. &amp;nbsp;I always wanted to keep it fairly simple and just have the red and white but I&#039;m glad we changed so I can be a little more crafty and not have to worry about the one colour being so consistent.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;So, here&#039;s the breakdown I have envisioned:&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Bridesmaides Dresses - Coral pink (already purchased, will post a pic in my next update)&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Suits - light-med grey pants and vest with white long-sleeved collared shirts. &amp;nbsp;Colin with a light pink tie (his request surprisingly) and the boys in a coral pink tie to match the BM dresses&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Flowers - Lilies &amp;amp; roses, unless I find something else that catches my eye. &amp;nbsp;Mostly white, (half of my bouquet, BM bouquets,&amp;nbsp;&lt;span&gt;boutonni\u00e8res and moms corsages. &amp;nbsp;Light pink and coral flowers for the other half of my bouquet, aisle flowers. &amp;nbsp;Combo of about 50% white, 50% pink mixture in decor flowers which I imagine at this point to only be at the reception table, head table, and for&amp;nbsp;centrepieces. &amp;nbsp;I&#039;d like to use the BM bouquets as reception decor, putting into vases but this will depend on timing with pictures etc and the overall reception decor.&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span&gt;Hits of metallic silver - Cake topper, my reception sandals (already purchased, need to post a pic),&amp;nbsp;centrepieces&amp;nbsp;(haven&#039;t decided on&amp;nbsp;these yet), frames for social media signage etc&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=\"color:rgb(40,40,40);font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"&gt;So far that&#039;s what i have pictured...&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span&gt;How does that sound?&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1904757,"PostDate":1442332391,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>@<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"281478\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/281478-perianjay\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">perianjay<\/span><\/a> I absolutely agree. \u00a0I always wanted to keep it fairly simple and just have the red and white but I'm glad we changed so I can be a little more crafty and not have to worry about the one colour being so consistent.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>So, here's the breakdown I have envisioned:<\/p>\n<p>Bridesmaides Dresses - Coral pink (already purchased, will post a pic in my next update)<\/p>\n<p>Suits - light-med grey pants and vest with white long-sleeved collared shirts. \u00a0Colin with a light pink tie (his request surprisingly) and the boys in a coral pink tie to match the BM dresses<\/p>\n<p>Flowers - Lilies & roses, unless I find something else that catches my eye. \u00a0Mostly white, (half of my bouquet, BM bouquets,\u00a0<span>boutonni\u00e8res and moms corsages. \u00a0Light pink and coral flowers for the other half of my bouquet, aisle flowers. \u00a0Combo of about 50% white, 50% pink mixture in decor flowers which I imagine at this point to only be at the reception table, head table, and for\u00a0centrepieces. \u00a0I'd like to use the BM bouquets as reception decor, putting into vases but this will depend on timing with pictures etc and the overall reception decor.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span>Hits of metallic silver - Cake topper, my reception sandals (already purchased, need to post a pic),\u00a0centrepieces\u00a0(haven't decided on\u00a0these yet), frames for social media signage etc<\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span  style=\"color:rgb(40,40,40);font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">So far that's what i have pictured...\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span>How does that sound?<\/span><\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<div><img src=\"http:\/\/\" alt=\"\"><\/div>\n<div><br><div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div><a  class=\"bbc_url\" href=\"http:\/\/www.TickerFactory.com\/\"><img src=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;10731;0\/st\/20160423\/e\/we+leave+for+Mexico%21\/k\/c059\/event.png\" alt=\"event.png\"><\/a>\u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0<a  class=\"bbc_url\" href=\"http:\/\/www.TickerFactory.com\/\"><img src=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;32;116\/st\/20160430\/e\/we+say+I+do%21\/k\/8afc\/event.png\" alt=\"event.png\"><\/a><\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>My Planning Thread:<\/p>\n<p><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79580-deecols-planning-thread-gbp-april-30th-2016\/#entry1904529'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79580-deecols-planning-thread-gbp-april-30th-2016\/#entry1904529<\/a>","Email":"deannaproteau@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"207.134.141.162","GroupId":3,"GroupName":"Member","JoinDate":1421446169,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-281751.jpg?_r=1455392044","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":222,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"deecol","Id":281751,"Name":"deecol","IsOnline":false}}],"Pages":{"TotalItems":308,"TotalPages":31,"CurrentPage":20,"NextPage":30,"PreviousPage":10,"LastPage":300},"PushNotifications":[{"Key":"notifications","Value":1,"Type":"int"},{"Key":"messages","Value":0,"Type":"int"}]}
